    <meta property="og:title" content={metaTitle} />
    <meta property="og:description" content={metaDescription} />
    <JsonLd graph={graph} />
  </head>
  <body>
    <SiteHeader />

    <main>
      <section
        class="page-header pillar-hero"
        style="--topic: rgba(241,94,74,0.16); --topic-fg: #d8412c;"
      >
        <div class="container">
          <div class="breadcrumbs">
            <a href="/">Home</a>
            <span>&#8250;</span>
            <a href="/seo">SEO</a>
            <span>&#8250;</span>
            <a href="/seo/backlinks">Link Building</a>
            <span>&#8250;</span>
            <span>Photography Posting Sites</span>
          </div>

          <span class="card-icon pillar-icon"><i class="fa-solid fa-camera-retro" aria-hidden="true"></i></span>
          <p class="eyebrow">Link building</p>
          <h1>{title}</h1>
          <p class="pillar-intro">{intro}</p>
          <PageByline />
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="content-body">
        <div class="container article-shell">
          <div class="prose pillar-body">
            <p class="prose-lede">Photography publishing splits into four tiers, and where you can land a byline depends on whether you have a portfolio to back it.</p>

            <p>The photo news and gear outlets do not take open guest posts. The education sites take tutorials from working photographers. The rumor and review blogs want hands-on testing. The fine-art platforms feature bodies of work. The list of 100 is below, grouped by tier.</p>

            <h2 id="tier">Pick your tier first</h2>
            <figure>
              <table>
                <thead>
                  <tr><th>Tier</th><th>Examples</th><th>How you get in</th></tr>
                </thead>
                <tbody>
                  <tr><td>Photo news &amp; gear</td><td>PetaPixel, DPReview, Fstoppers, Digital Camera World, B&amp;H Explora</td><td>Not open guest posts. Exclusive news, original test data, or a strong tutorial with a portfolio</td></tr>
                  <tr><td>Education &amp; tutorials</td><td>Digital Photography School, Photography Life, SLR Lounge, CreativeLive, Cambridge in Colour</td><td>Tutorials from working photographers, with your own example images and settings</td></tr>
                  <tr><td>Rumor &amp; review blogs</td><td>Nikon Rumors, Canon Rumors, Fuji Rumors, Sony Alpha Rumors, PhotographyBlog</td><td>Hands-on testing, sample files, gear analysis</td></tr>
                  <tr><td>Fine-art &amp; portfolio</td><td>Magnum, Aperture, LensCulture, Feature Shoot, This Is Colossal</td><td>A cohesive body of work and a project statement</td></tr>
                </tbody>
              </table>
            </figure>

            <h2 id="metrics">What the metrics mean</h2>
            <figure>
              <table>
                <thead>
                  <tr><th>Metric</th><th>What it is</th><th>How much it matters</th></tr>
                </thead>
                <tbody>
                  <tr><td>Domain Rating (DR)</td><td>Ahrefs' 0 to 100 score for a whole site's backlink profile</td><td>A useful filter, not a verdict</td></tr>
                  <tr><td>Domain Authority (DA)</td><td>Moz's equivalent 0 to 100 score</td><td>Same idea as DR</td></tr>
                  <tr><td>Page Authority (PA)</td><td>Moz's score for one specific page</td><td>Matters once you know which page your post will live on</td></tr>
                  <tr><td>URL Rating (UR)</td><td>Ahrefs' score for one specific URL</td><td>Same purpose as PA</td></tr>
                  <tr><td>Monthly Traffic</td><td>Estimated organic visits per month</td><td>The most honest signal that a link will be seen</td></tr>
                </tbody>
              </table>
            </figure>

            <div class="callout"><p><strong>Here is the deal:</strong> photography content is judged on the images. A tutorial on a mid-DR site with your own strong example photos is worth more than a link from a higher-DR site where your work is not shown.</p></div>

            <h2 id="list">The 100 photography sites</h2>
            <p>Domain Rating, Domain Authority, Page Authority, URL Rating and estimated monthly traffic. Every domain was checked live in September 2026; closed sites were replaced with live equivalents. Metrics are third-party estimates and shift over time.</p>
            <figure>
              <table>
                <thead>
                  <tr><th>#</th><th>Website</th><th>DR</th><th>DA</th><th>PA</th><th>UR</th><th>Monthly traffic</th></tr>
                </thead>
                <tbody>
                  {SITES.map((s) => (
                    <tr>
                      <td>{s.n}</td>
                      <td>{s.site}</td>
                      <td>{s.dr}</td>
                      <td>{s.da}</td>
                      <td>{s.pa}</td>
                      <td>{s.ur}</td>
                      <td>{s.traffic}</td>
                    </tr>
                  ))}
                </tbody>
              </table>
            </figure>

            <h2 id="pitch">The pitch that works for photography editors</h2>
            <ol>
              <li><strong>Lead with the image or the finding.</strong> "How I shot this in one exposure" or "we tested 6 50mm lenses on the same scene" earns the read.</li>
              <li><strong>Show the portfolio.</strong> A link to your work in the pitch. Editors will not take a tutorial from someone whose photos they cannot see.</li>
              <li><strong>Pitch the section.</strong> "For your landscape tutorials" or "for the gear reviews" shows you read the site.</li>
              <li><strong>Bring your own assets.</strong> Full-res samples, RAW files, a settings table, before-and-after edits.</li>
              <li><strong>Match the format.</strong> News wants a tight story. Education sites want a structured how-to. Fine-art platforms want a project.</li>
              <li><strong>Disclose any brand or sponsorship</strong> behind the gear you are writing about.</li>
            </ol>
            <div class="callout"><p><strong>The test:</strong> would an editor run this if you sold no prints or presets? If yes, pitch it. If it is a promo for your Lightroom pack, it goes in the bin.</p></div>

            <h2 id="mistakes">What not to do</h2>
            <ul class="check-list">
              <li>Pitch a "best camera for beginners" listicle with no testing.</li>
              <li>Illustrate a tutorial with stock images instead of your own.</li>
              <li>Send the same pitch to a photo-news site and a fine-art platform.</li>
              <li>Stuff affiliate links, or point exact-match anchors ("best mirrorless camera") at your store.</li>
              <li>Use AI-generated "photography tips" with no images and no photographer behind them.</li>
            </ul>
            <div class="callout"><p><strong>Bottom line:</strong> a few placements on sites whose readers shoot your genre, with your own images shown, will do more for rankings and bookings than a long list of thin photo-blog links. Use this list to find your few.</p></div>
          </div>

          <aside class="article-toc">
            <h4>On this page</h4>
            <ul>
              {toc.map((item) => (
                <li><a href={`#${item.id}`}>{item.text}</a></li>
              ))}
            </ul>
          </aside>
        </div>
      </section>

      <div id="faq">
        <Faq items={faqs} />
      </div>

      <section class="section section-alt">
        <div class="container">
          <div class="cta-panel" style="text-align: center; max-width: 720px; margin: 0 auto;">
            <h2>Want us to run the outreach?</h2>
            <p>
              We build the shortlist by genre, package your best work and test data, write the pitches
              and place them on real photography publications. No link farms, no risk.
            </p>
            <div class="hero-actions" style="justify-content: center; margin-top: 0;">
              <a href="/services" class="button">View services</a>
              <a
                href={whatsappUrl("Hi SERP Mentor, I would like help with photography guest posting and digital PR.")}
                class="button-secondary"
                target="_blank"
                rel="noopener noreferrer"
              >
                <i class="fa-brands fa-whatsapp" aria-hidden="true"></i> WhatsApp
              </a>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>
    </main>

    <SiteFooter />
  </body>
</html>
